# Documentation Authority

When code and a document disagree, the document wins.

Order: `AGENTS.md`, then `docs/PRODUCT_PRD.md`, `docs/TECHNICAL_PRD.md`, `docs/DATA_SOURCES.md`, `docs/DATABASE_DESIGN.md`, `docs/AUTHENTICATION.md`, `docs/API_CONTRACT.md`, `docs/AI_RAG_DESIGN.md`, `docs/UI_UX_DESIGN.md`, `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, then code.

## Conflict protocol

Do not silently change an approved decision.

1. Name the document and the statement.
2. Say why the conflict matters.
3. Propose the smallest change.
4. Wait for approval before editing the source document.

Then update anything downstream so the docs still agree.

## Do not drift

Do not add a feature, source, column, or endpoint in a code change that the docs do not already allow. A meaningful architecture change is written into the owning document first.
